Subject: [PATCH] feat: add worker blueprints with runtime integration

X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: enable reusable worker blueprints with coordinator policy, generated tools, and bounded paginated output
X-Jcode-Patch-Kind: personal-feature
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: 0001-candidate-pre-tool-input-transformers.patch, 1001-personal-release-installer-path-opt-in.patch, 1002-personal-provider-family-allowlist.patch, 1003-personal-feature-configure-session-picker-sorting.patch, 1004-personal-feature-configure-session-picker-default-filter.patch, 1005-personal-feature-delete-sessions-from-picker.patch, 1006-personal-openrouter-eu.patch, 1007-personal-feature-disable-telemetry-delivery-and-remove-telemetry-controls.patch, 1008-personal-feature-remove-hosted-subscription-and-promotional-commands.patch, 1009-personal-feature-remove-promotional-onboarding-content.patch, 1010-personal-feature-remove-sponsored-integration-discovery.patch, 1011-personal-feature-disable-automatic-onboarding.patch, 1012-personal-feature-remove-hosted-account-cli-commands.patch, 1013-personal-feature-remove-hosted-account-tui-commands.patch, 1014-personal-feature-docs-remove-sponsored-discovery-documentation.patch, 1015-personal-feature-refactor-remove-hosted-subscription-account-api.patch, 1016-personal-feature-docs-remove-hosted-account-and-cloud-documentation.patch, 1017-personal-feature-refactor-route-jcode-choice-through-direct-endpoin.patch, 1018-personal-feature-allow-selecting-the-self-update-repository.patch

Patch intent:
Add a worker blueprint system that lets a jcode user define reusable,
specialized subagent roles in Markdown. Each blueprint supplies durable role
instructions, model, effort, allowed-tools, communication-policy, and timeout.
At runtime, every valid blueprint generates a coordinator-visible tool named
swarm_<id> that spawns a blueprint-backed worker, waits for completion, and
returns a compact summary with paginated follow-up reads. Runtime resolution
uses the documented default blueprint directory, including symlinked directories
and Markdown files, and rejects nonblank blueprint IDs that are unavailable or
invalid instead of spawning a generic worker. A
coordinator-only tool policy (agents.coordinator) restricts the coordinator's
own tools without affecting internal roles or spawned workers.

Why it exists:
Worker blueprints let a user specialize subagents without code changes. A
blueprint can pin a cheap model for routine work, restrict its tool access,
control its communication, and cap its runtime. The generated tool returns a
bounded summary (2000 chars) so the coordinator does not burn tokens reading
the worker's full output. A deterministic follow-up read (no LLM) lets the
coordinator page through more output in 2000-char chunks when needed. The
coordinator policy lets a user remove broad tools like bash and generic swarm
from the coordinator while retaining them for authorized specialized workers
and internal agents. When the swarm feature is off, swarm and generated swarm_<id> tools are omitted from the session tool surface and rejected at execution, the root coordinator has no coordinator-specific tool limit applied or exposed, and swarm-specific agent settings are omitted from the config summary. Runtime toggles remove and restore that coordinator policy while preserving global tool limits.

Upstream integration points:
- crates/jcode-config-types/src/lib.rs: CoordinatorConfig struct,
  swarm_timeout_minutes field, timeout_minutes on WorkerBlueprintOverride,
  coordinator and worker_blueprints fields on AgentsConfig.
- crates/jcode-base/src/config.rs: re-exports CoordinatorConfig.
- crates/jcode-base/src/worker_blueprint.rs: blueprint discovery from the
  documented ~/.jcode/worker-blueprints/ default, including symlinked files and
  directories, front-matter parsing, schema validation, override merging,
  diagnostics, and Display impl for WorkerBlueprintDiagnostic.
- crates/jcode-protocol/src/wire.rs: blueprint field on CommSpawn.
- crates/jcode-app-core/src/agent.rs: apply_coordinator_policy applied to root
  sessions in new_with_initial_ownership, with swarm-disabled bypass.
- crates/jcode-app-core/src/agent/turn_execution.rs: set_swarm_enabled refreshes
  the root session policy when the feature is toggled at runtime.
- crates/jcode-app-core/src/server/comm_session.rs: fallible blueprint
  resolution that rejects requested unavailable or invalid IDs, prompt
  composition, tool policy application, communication policy storage in
  spawn_swarm_agent.
- crates/jcode-app-core/src/server/client_comm_message.rs: communication
  policy enforcement in handle_comm_message.
- crates/jcode-app-core/src/server/state.rs: communication_policy field on
  SwarmMember.
- crates/jcode-app-core/src/tool/blueprint.rs: BlueprintTool implementing the
  Tool trait. Generated tools default to headless workers so synchronous
  calls cannot hang on a separate headed client attachment; explicit spawn
  modes remain honored. Spawn mode: spawn, await, return compact summary
  with session ID. Follow-up mode: deterministic paginated read of stored
  output. Timeout
  resolved per-call > blueprint > config > default (20m).
- crates/jcode-app-core/src/tool/tests.rs: excludes user-owned generated
  swarm_<id> descriptions from the static built-in tool-description token cap.
- crates/jcode-app-core/src/tool/mod.rs: register_blueprint_tools in
  Registry::new.
- crates/jcode-app-core/src/tool/communicate.rs: blueprint field in
  CommunicateInput and spawn action.
- crates/jcode-app-core/src/tool/communicate/transport.rs: send_request and
  send_request_with_timeout made pub(crate) for blueprint tool reuse.

Update guidance:
Preserve the documented ~/.jcode/worker-blueprints/ default, including
symlinked directories and Markdown files, and reject every nonblank requested
blueprint ID that cannot resolve. Preserve the precedence chain for model
(per-spawn > blueprint > swarm_model > coordinator) and timeout (per-call >
blueprint > config > default 20m). Generated swarm_<id> descriptions are
user-owned and exempt from the static built-in description token cap. Blueprint
allowed-tools are always intersected with the global tool policy. Coordinator
policy only applies to root sessions, never to spawned workers or internal
roles. Communication-policy: none blocks ordinary messages but not tool
results. Generated tools default to headless execution when spawn mode is omitted or
set to auto, unless the caller explicitly selects another spawn mode, so their
synchronous result wait cannot depend on a headed client attaching to a new
persisted session. Generated
tools never overwrite existing tool names. All test
SwarmMember and WorkerBlueprintOverride constructions must include the new
fields.

